#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/subplot.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.subplot.subplot:91
msgid ""
"[*side*]\\ *clearance*. Reserve a space of dimension *clearance* between the "
"margin and the subplot on the specified side, using *side* values from "
"**w**, **e**, **s**, or **n**; or **x** for both **w** and **e**; or **y** "
"for both **s** and **n**. No *side* means all sides (i.e. "
"``clearance=\"1c\"`` would set a clearance of 1 cm on all sides). The option "
"is repeatable to set aside space on more than one side (e.g. "
"``clearance=[\"w1c\", \"s2c\"]`` would set a clearance of 1 cm on west side "
"and 2 cm on south side). Such space will be left untouched by the main "
"plotting but can be accessed by methods that plot scales, bars, text, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/subplot.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.subplot.subplot:104
msgid ""
"Margin space that is added between neighboring subplots (i.e., the interior "
"margins) in addition to the automatic space added for tick marks, "
"annotations, and labels. The margins can be specified as either:  - a single "
"value (for same margin on all sides). E.g. ``\"5c\"``. - a pair of values "
"(for separate horizontal and vertical margins). E.g.,   ``(\"5c\", "
"\"3c\")``. - a set of four values (for separate left, right, bottom, and top "
"margins).   E.g., ``(\"1c\", \"2c\", \"3c\", \"4c\")``.  The actual gap "
"created is always a sum of the margins for the two opposing sides (e.g., "
"east plus west or south plus north margins) [Default is half the primary "
"annotation font size, giving the full annotation font size as the default "
"gap]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/subplot.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.subplot.subplot:104
msgid ""
"Margin space that is added between neighboring subplots (i.e., the interior "
"margins) in addition to the automatic space added for tick marks, "
"annotations, and labels. The margins can be specified as either:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/subplot.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.subplot.subplot:108
msgid "a single value (for same margin on all sides). E.g. ``\"5c\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/subplot.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.subplot.subplot:109
msgid ""
"a pair of values (for separate horizontal and vertical margins). E.g., "
"``(\"5c\", \"3c\")``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/subplot.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.subplot.subplot:111
msgid ""
"a set of four values (for separate left, right, bottom, and top margins). E."
"g., ``(\"1c\", \"2c\", \"3c\", \"4c\")``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/subplot.py:docstring
